menu "pw_assert"

config PIGWEED_ASSERT_PIGWEED_OVERRIDES
    bool
    select ASSERT_CUSTOM_HEADER
    help
      Map all the Zephyr assert macros to use Pigweed's PW_ASSERT* macros, so
      that all asserts are consumed by the same assert backend, provided by the
      user. The user must also provide the assert backend header indirection.

choice PIGWEED_ASSERT_BACKEND
    prompt "pw_assert.assert / pw_assert.check backend used"
    default PIGWEED_ASSERT_ZEPHYR
    help
      What PW_ASSERT()/PW_CHECK()/PW_CRASH() do when they fire. Defaults to
      Zephyr's assert. Choose "none" to provide your own backend.

config PIGWEED_ASSERT_ZEPHYR
    bool "Link pw_assert_zephyr library"
    select PIGWEED_PREPROCESSOR
    help
      Routes Pigweed's own PW_ASSERT()/PW_CHECK()/PW_CRASH() into Zephyr's
      assert subsystem: a failure calls, in order, ``__ASSERT_LOC()``, then
      (if there's a message) ``__ASSERT_MSG_INFO()``, then
      ``__ASSERT_POST_ACTION()``. This is one-directional -- only Pigweed's
      own assert macros are affected. Zephyr's own native ``__ASSERT()``
      call sites elsewhere in the kernel and subsystems are untouched and
      keep behaving however Zephyr's own CONFIG_ASSERT/CONFIG_ASSERT_LEVEL
      configure them. See :ref:`module-pw_assert` for module details.

config PIGWEED_ASSERT_TOKENIZED
    bool "Maps all Zephyr assert macros to use pw_assert_tokenized as the backend"
    select PIGWEED_ASSERT_PIGWEED_OVERRIDES
    select PIGWEED_PREPROCESSOR
    select PIGWEED_TOKENIZER
    help
      Does two things:

      1. Redirects Zephyr's own native assert macros (the ones Zephyr's
         kernel and subsystems call internally) to go through Pigweed's
         PW_ASSERT()/PW_CHECK() instead of Zephyr's own assert subsystem
         (this is what PIGWEED_ASSERT_PIGWEED_OVERRIDES, selected above,
         does via ASSERT_CUSTOM_HEADER).
      2. Sets :ref:`module-pw_assert_tokenized` as the backend for
         PW_ASSERT()/PW_CHECK()/PW_CRASH() themselves (Pigweed's own calls,
         and -- because of (1) -- what used to be Zephyr's own asserts
         too), so every one of them gets tokenized and forwarded to the log
         system instead of calling into Zephyr's assert subsystem.

      The tokenizer handler should check for ``LOG_LEVEL_FATAL`` and
      properly divert to a crash handler. Make sure an appropriate
      PIGWEED_LOG_TOKENIZED* configuration is set.

config PIGWEED_ASSERT_NONE
    bool "Provide your own pw_assert.assert/pw_assert.check backend"
    help
      Pigweed's Zephyr backend is not linked in. Wire up your own via
      pw_set_backend() or an equivalent mechanism.

endchoice

endmenu
